less - browse text a screen at a time

SYNOPSIS
    less [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Display each file in order. With no operands, read standard input.
    A dash operand also reads standard input. On a terminal, the display
    uses the console viewport. For piped input, less reads ahead as
    needed and uses /dev/console for keys. Redirecting standard output
    copies the input as plain text.

    Down and Up or j and k move one line. Page Down or Space moves
    forward one screen. Page Up or b moves back a screen. Home or g
    jumps to the start. End or G reads to the end, subject to the
    one MiB buffer. Press q to leave the current file.

EXAMPLES
    less /README /LICENSE
    seq 100 | less

SEE ALSO
    cat(1), man(1), stty(1)
